WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:16.562
The next day a strange thing happened in the attic.

2
00:00:16.563 --> 00:00:21.362
Sara was out doing errands as usual.

3
00:00:21.363 --> 00:00:26.133
So Mel the rat was the only one who saw and heard what happened.

4
00:00:26.134 --> 00:00:31.596
Mel had left his hole and was looking for food in Sara's room.

5
00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:36.406
Suddenly he heard a noise on the roof.

6
00:00:36.407 --> 00:00:40.651
Two men opened the skylight and then peered through it.

7
00:00:40.652 --> 00:00:44.972
One man was Ram Dass, the Indian servant from next door.

8
00:00:44.973 --> 00:00:50.377
The other was a young man—Mr. Carrisford's secretary.

9
00:00:50.378 --> 00:00:54.481
Mel watched the two men enter the room through the skylight.

10
00:00:54.482 --> 00:00:57.822
Neither one made a sound.

11
00:00:57.823 --> 00:01:03.230
Mel was used to Sara by now, but the two strangers frightened him.

12
00:01:03.231 --> 00:01:07.678
He ran into his hole, but he kept an eye on the two men.

13
00:01:07.679 --> 00:01:11.405
The secretary had caught a glimpse of Mel's tail.

14
00:01:11.406 --> 00:01:15.450
"Was that a rat?" he whispered to Ram Dass.

15
00:01:15.451 --> 00:01:22.346
"Yes," Ram Dass whispered back. "There are many rats living in these walls."

16
00:01:22.347 --> 00:01:25.400
"Ugh!" exclaimed the young man.

17
00:01:25.401 --> 00:01:29.494
"I'm surprised the girl is not terrified by them."

18
00:01:29.495 --> 00:01:33.297
"She's not like other children," replied Ram Dass.

19
00:01:33.298 --> 00:01:36.339
"She's a friend to all living creatures.

20
00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:41.148
I often watch her from my skylight and see her talking to the birds.

21
00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:45.669
She's kind to humans too," Ram Dass went on.

22
00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:49.623
"The servant girl in the next room comes to her for comfort.

23
00:01:49.624 --> 00:01:53.386
Then there is a blond girl who comes to hear her stories.

24
00:01:53.387 --> 00:01:56.545
And a little girl who worships her.

25
00:01:56.546 --> 00:01:59.680
The mistress of the house treats her like an outcast.

26
00:01:59.681 --> 00:02:03.583
But the girl acts like she comes from a family of kings.

27
00:02:03.584 --> 00:02:06.554
She's a true princess!"

28
00:02:06.555 --> 00:02:10.866
"You seem to know a lot about her," the secretary said.

29
00:02:10.867 --> 00:02:15.897
Ram Dass nodded. "I watch her closely," he said.

30
00:02:15.898 --> 00:02:20.351
"Are you sure she won't come up here now?" the secretary asked.

31
00:02:20.352 --> 00:02:23.232
"If she finds us, she'll be frightened.

32
00:02:23.233 --> 00:02:26.391
And it would spoil Mr. Carrisford's plans."

33
00:02:26.392 --> 00:02:33.021
"She has gone out and probably won't return for hours," said Ram Dass.

34
00:02:33.022 --> 00:02:36.367
"Besides, I can hear anyone on the stairs.

35
00:02:36.368 --> 00:02:39.278
We'll have time to escape if necessary."

36
00:02:39.279 --> 00:02:43.100
The secretary took a pencil and paper from his pocket.

37
00:02:43.101 --> 00:02:46.936
"Keep your ears open."

38
00:02:46.937 --> 00:02:52.405
He began to walk slowly around the miserable little room, making notes.

39
00:02:52.406 --> 00:02:57.635
First he went to the narrow bed. He pressed his hand on the mattress.

40
00:02:57.636 --> 00:03:01.445
"Hard as a rock!" he exclaimed.

41
00:03:01.446 --> 00:03:05.109
"The blanket is thin and the sheets are ragged."

42
00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:08.128
Then he looked at the dark fireplace.

43
00:03:08.129 --> 00:03:11.932
"There hasn't been a fire there for days."

44
00:03:11.933 --> 00:03:15.589
"I've never seen a fire there," said Ram Dass.

45
00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.924
"It's always freezing in here.

46
00:03:17.925 --> 00:03:22.409
I don't believe the mistress cares how cold the girl gets."

47
00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:27.355
"What a place for a child to sleep in!" said the secretary.

48
00:03:27.356 --> 00:03:34.395
He noted the old table and bare floor. "Whose idea was it to help her?"

49
00:03:34.396 --> 00:03:37.534
"It was mine," said Ram Dass.

50
00:03:37.535 --> 00:03:40.791
"I like to hear the stories she tells her friends.

51
00:03:40.792 --> 00:03:46.104
One night she pretended this room was warm, comfortable, and filled with beautiful things."

52
00:03:46.105 --> 00:03:50.149
Ram Dass had repeated Sara's story to Mr. Carrisford.

53
00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:54.728
The sick gentleman had not liked the way she was treated at the school.

54
00:03:54.729 --> 00:03:58.817
He began to think about making her dreams come true.

55
00:03:58.818 --> 00:04:04.151
"Do you think we can transform this room while she sleeps?" the secretary asked.

56
00:04:04.152 --> 00:04:08.291
"Of course we'd have to replace her bed during the day."

57
00:04:08.292 --> 00:04:13.496
"I can do it all with the help of another servant," Ram Dass replied.

58
00:04:13.497 --> 00:04:16.401
"We'll be so quiet that she won't wake up.

59
00:04:16.402 --> 00:04:20.954
When she does awake, she will think that a magician has been here!"

60
00:04:20.955 --> 00:04:24.370
The secretary continued looking around.

61
00:04:24.371 --> 00:04:31.640
He made notes about the floor, the fireplace, the broken footstool, and the old table.

62
00:04:31.641 --> 00:04:37.328
He also remarked that a number of old nails had been placed in the walls.

63
00:04:37.329 --> 00:04:39.961
Ram Dass smiled mysteriously.

64
00:04:39.962 --> 00:04:44.975
"Yesterday when she was out, I entered the room, bringing with me some sharp nails.

65
00:04:44.976 --> 00:04:48.471
I pressed them into the walls, where we will need them."

66
00:04:48.472 --> 00:04:53.665
The secretary nodded. "You can hang things on them," he said.

67
00:04:53.666 --> 00:04:56.202
Soon the men were finished.

68
00:04:56.203 --> 00:05:01.626
"I think I've made enough notes. We can go now," said the secretary.

69
00:05:01.627 --> 00:05:05.991
"It's a shame Mr. Carrisford has not found that lost child.

70
00:05:05.992 --> 00:05:08.519
He has such a warm heart."

71
00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:12.090
"If he finds her, his strength will return.

72
00:05:12.091 --> 00:05:17.701
He will be well again," said Ram Dass. "I'm sure of that."

73
00:05:17.702 --> 00:05:23.471
Then the two men slipped silently through the skylight and across the roof.

74
00:05:23.472 --> 00:05:28.150
After Mel was sure they had gone, he came out of his hole.

75
00:05:28.151 --> 00:05:30.591
He sniffed around the floor.

76
00:05:30.592 --> 00:05:33.857
He didn't understand what the men had talked about.

77
00:05:33.858 --> 00:05:41.818
But he hoped they had dropped some crumbs.
